From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:14:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ship the bundled Redis server's licence texts in the
 wheel

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every redislite wheel on PyPI, so it needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

The wheel bundles redis-server and redis-cli, compiled from Redis
6.2.14 together with its vendored hiredis, linenoise, Lua and
hdr_histogram, but carries only redislite's own LICENSE.txt. Their
BSD/MIT licences require the copyright notice to travel with binary
redistribution. The singular license_file key disables setuptools'
default licence glob, so list every file explicitly; jemalloc is not
listed because the build uses MALLOC=libc.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index 105c8a7..3b51c40 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -26,7 +26,14 @@ classifiers =
 description = Redis built into a python package
 keywords = redis sqlite python service integrated
 license = BSD License
-license_file = LICENSE.txt
+license_files =
+    LICENSE.txt
+    redis.submodule/COPYING
+    redis.submodule/deps/hiredis/COPYING
+    redis.submodule/deps/linenoise/linenoise.h
+    redis.submodule/deps/lua/COPYRIGHT
+    redis.submodule/deps/hdr_histogram/LICENSE.txt
+    redis.submodule/deps/hdr_histogram/COPYING.txt
 long_description = file:README.md
 long_description_content_type = text/markdown
 name = redislite
-- 
